| `layers.backend.python` | string | the copier answer `backend_python` (`>=3.10`) | a version specifier equal to `pyproject.toml` `requires-python`; floor major and minor parts fully match `[0-9]{1,4}` | check_H; the parse deferral in `scripts/check_structure.py` `_declared_python_floor` | A value that differs from `requires-python` is a check_H error. Under an interpreter older than its floor, a `.py` file that does not parse is deferred to `make check-all` with one warning instead of an error; with no floor to read it is an error. Superscript, non-ASCII or overlong numeric floor parts give one finding and exit CONFIG. | the interpreter make runs: the make variable `PY` | always |
